# App Router conventions

## Server vs Client components

- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only when the file uses hooks, refs, or browser APIs (event handlers count).
- Keep data fetching in Server Components / route handlers; never in atoms.

## Layout & PWA

- `app/layout.tsx` is the only place to mount providers (`ThemeProvider`, future `TooltipProvider`).
- Always export both `metadata` and `viewport` — `viewportFit: "cover"` is required for safe-area to work.
- Use `min-h-dvh` (not `min-h-screen`) so iOS reports the correct viewport height.
- Wrap top-level shells with the safe-area utilities (`pt-safe`, `pb-safe`, `px-safe`).

## Fonts & icons

- Fonts come from `next/font` only — never `<link>` tags. Geist for sans, Geist_Mono for mono.
- Icons come from `@/lib/icons`, never directly from `lucide-react` in app code.

## Routing

- Co-locate `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, and `not-found.tsx` per route segment.
- Route Handlers live in `app/api/*/route.ts`.
